       en="**σπεύδω** (learned: hasten; aor. *έσπευσα*) is typical of written narrative: *έσπευσαν να βοηθήσουν* “rushed to help”. Everyday equivalents: *έτρεξαν να βοηθήσουν*, *βιάστηκαν να…* (with a nuance of haste, sometimes negative). The subjunctive after *να* is perfective for a single action.",
